ation"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/655"} "Jang-chung Che-yuk-gwan, Seoul"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/16446"} "36 from 36 countries"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Format"] [:td {:colspan "2"} "Two single-elimination pools, with winner of each pool advanced to the final. All judoka losing to the winner of each pool advanced to repêchage pools, with the winners of the repêchage pools earning bronze medals."]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "The two favorites were Japan’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/33838"} "Shinji Hosokawa"] " and Korea’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/33915"} "Kim Jae-Yeop"] ". Hosokawa had won the 1984 gold medal and the 1985 World Championship. Kim was the silver medalist in 1984, and had won the 1987 Worlds, defeating Hosokawa in the final. Kim made his way to the final with no difficulties. Hosokawa met " [:a {:href "/athletes/33431"} "Kevin Asano"] " (USA) in the pool final. Asano had been bronze medalist at the 1987 World Championships. Both used several varieties of " [:em {} "tomoe-nage"] " and both eluded being thrown throughout the match. The two judges split, giving the decision to the referee who advanced Asano to the final. The final was very close. Kim eventually won the gold medal, but only by a late " [:em {} "shido"] " given to Asano for passivity. The Korean crowd was wildly ecstatic, and when Kim appeared for the medal ceremony, it was in traditional Korean dress."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/33915"} "Kim Jae-Yeop"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/KOR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/KOR.png"}] "KOR"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athle